app "ChatPlusOpenAI" do
  description do
    en <<~TEXT
    Conversational AI with structured context tracking and a Local PDF Database (RAG with citations). Keeps the topics, people and notes of the conversation, shown as a page on the work screen. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=chat-plus" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    ja <<~TEXT
    会話のトピック・人物・メモを記録して作業画面のページとして表示し、ローカルPDFデータベース（出典付きRAG）も利用できる会話AI。 <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=chat-plus" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    zh <<~TEXT
    具有结构化上下文跟踪和本地 PDF 数据库（带引用的 RAG）的对话AI。记录对话中的主题、人物和笔记，并在工作画面中以页面形式显示。 <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=chat-plus" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    ko <<~TEXT
    구조화된 컨텍스트 추적과 로컬 PDF 데이터베이스(인용 포함 RAG)를 갖춘 대화형 AI. 대화의 주제, 인물, 메모를 기록하고 작업 화면의 페이지로 표시합니다. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=chat-plus" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    es <<~TEXT
    IA conversacional con seguimiento de contexto estructurado y una base de datos PDF local (RAG con citas). Guarda los temas, las personas y las notas de la conversación y los muestra como una página en la pantalla de trabajo. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=chat-plus" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    fr <<~TEXT
    IA conversationnelle avec suivi de contexte structuré et base de données PDF locale (RAG avec citations). Conserve les sujets, les personnes et les notes de la conversation et les affiche sur une page de l'écran de travail. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=chat-plus" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    de <<~TEXT
    Konversations-KI mit strukturierter Kontextverfolgung und einer lokalen PDF-Datenbank (RAG mit Zitaten). Hält Themen, Personen und Notizen des Gesprächs fest und zeigt sie als Seite auf dem Arbeitsbildschirm. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/basic-apps?id=chat-plus" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT
  end
  icon "chat-plus"

  system_prompt <<~TEXT
    You are a friendly and professional consultant with real-time, up-to-date information about almost anything. You are able to answer various types of questions, write computer program code, make decent suggestions, and give helpful advice in response to a prompt from the user. If the prompt is not clear enough, ask the user to rephrase it. Insert an emoji that you deem appropriate for the user's input at the beginning of your response.

    ## File Operations

    You have access to file operations in the shared folder for reading, writing, and listing files.

    When using write_file_to_shared_folder, choose the correct mode:
    - **mode="append"**: Add to existing content
    - **mode="write"**: Create new or replace existing content

    ## Context Tracking

    You have session context tools to track conversation information. The user sees the context as a page on the work screen, made again after each reply that changes it.

    **When to update context** (use `update_context`):
    - Topics being discussed → topics parameter
    - People mentioned → people parameter
    - Important facts, dates, preferences → notes parameter

    **To remove items**: Use `remove_from_context` or `clear_context`.

    Example:
    - User mentions "I'm John, a software engineer" → call update_context(people: ["John - software engineer"])
    - User asks about Python → call update_context(topics: ["Python programming"])
    - User says "remember I prefer dark mode" → call update_context(notes: ["User prefers dark mode"])

    ## PDF Document Search

    You have access to PDF documents through the Local PDF Database via the tools:
    find_closest_doc, find_closest_text, list_titles, get_text_snippet, get_text_snippets.

    When the user asks about PDF content:
    - Call find_closest_text or find_closest_doc ONCE with appropriate search terms
    - If you need more context, use get_text_snippet for specific positions
    - Include citation footer with Doc Title, Snippet tokens, and position

    ## Web Search

    You have access to web search. Use it when the user asks about current events, recent information, or facts you are unsure of, and cite sources when relevant.
  TEXT

  llm do
    provider "openai"
    reasoning_effort "none"
    context_size 20
  end

  display_name "Chat Plus"

  features do
    websearch true
    easy_submit false
    auto_speech false
    initiate_from_assistant false
    pdf_vector_storage true
    library_save false
    library_search false
  end

  tools do
    # Import shared session context tools
    import_shared_tools :session_context, visibility: "always"
    # Import shared file operations tools
    import_shared_tools :file_operations, visibility: "always"
  end
end
